#!/usr/bin/env perl
use 5.020;
use strict;
use warnings;
use Ham::QSO::_Internal::CLI;
local $SIG{PIPE} = 'IGNORE' if exists $SIG{PIPE};
exit Ham::QSO::_Internal::CLI::run(\@ARGV, \*STDIN, \*STDOUT, \*STDERR);

=encoding UTF-8

=head1 NAME

ham-qso - strict QSO message analysis, evidence replay and CW/RTTY integration

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    ham-qso compose --station IU0ABC --kind cq
    ham-qso parse --json 'IU0ABC DE DL1ABC RST 579 KN'
    ham-qso replay --station IU0ABC --input examples/complete-it-cw.jsonl --strict
    ham-qso encode 'CQ DE IU0ABC K'
    ham-qso wav --output practice.wav 'CQ DE IU0ABC K'
    ham-qso profiles --profile it-rtty
    ham-qso help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

See C<ham-qso help> for command options. Default profile is it-cw. Core commands
require no codec or PDL. encode/decode/wav/receive load the selected optional
Ham::CW or Ham::RTTY. All output goes to stdout unless --output is supplied;
diagnostics go to stderr. Existing paths require explicit --overwrite. Inputs
are bounded to 16 MiB and each message to 8192 characters. Replay takes one JSON
object per line with the Session feed schema, or operator select_peer/abort records.
No command operates a radio, microphone or playback device.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

0 success; 1 with --strict for unsupported/ambiguous/violating analysis, uncertain
audio, or incomplete/nonconforming replay; 2 invalid arguments, missing optional
dependencies or input/output failure. Checked scope is reported explicitly;
success never certifies complete compliance with Italian or international law.

